{
  "title": "Clients keep cached rows the server no longer has after a restore",
  "description": "When a client syncs with a cursor this database never issued (a restore from an older backup), both sync endpoints answer as a full sync: every live row plus every deletion (db::valid_since; recipe sync and shopping-list sync). \
Neither client prunes on that answer: iOS RecipeCacheStore.apply and ShoppingListStore, and web shoppingListSyncCache.ts, only upsert and apply tombstones. \
A row created after the backup was taken exists on the client but in neither the server's rows nor its tombstones, so it lingers in the client cache forever (iOS offline search keeps finding a recipe the server doesn't have). \
Fix: have the server flag such a response (e.g. `full_resync: true`) and have web and iOS replace their cache with it, with tests on both clients and an e2e test. \
Only matters after restoring an older backup.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
